WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:32.458
<b>In the previous verse, Sri Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:36.041
<b>that a true scholar is one whose every</b>
<b>action is free from self-interest,</b>

3
00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:43.208
<b>and who has burned the fruits of his</b>
<b>actions in the fire of divine knowledge.</b>

4
00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:45.041
<b>This is a form of 'actionless action' or 'Akarma',</b>

5
00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:49.666
<b>which was mentioned in the earlier </b>
<b>verses of this chapter.</b>

6
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:56.500
<b>This verse now illuminates the behavior that </b>
<b>transforms one's actions into actionless action.</b>

7
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:02.333
<b>Those who walk this path incorporate </b>
<b>these principles into their life's journey.</b>

8
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Sri Krishna proclaims:</b>

9
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.208
<b>By completely releasing attachment </b>
<b>to the fruits of his actions,</b>

10
00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:15.291
<b>a wise person always remains </b>
<b>consistently content.</b>

11
00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:22.250
<b>This contentment does not depend on any </b>
<b>external object, person, or circumstance.</b>

12
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:29.250
<b>Such an individual performs various actions</b>
<b>without truly being bound by them.</b>

13
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:36.375
<b>Krishna is presenting an ideal </b>
<b>approach to acting and living.</b>

14
00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:39.083
<b>"Tyaktva Karma-Phalasangam" –</b>

15
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.250
<b>Means performing actions without attachment.</b>

16
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.083
<b>This is the core concept of this verse.</b>

17
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:51.500
<b>In life, this translates to fulfilling all </b>
<b>duties with absolute dedication,</b>

18
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.166
<b>without becoming attached to what </b>
<b>might be received in return.</b>

19
00:01:56.166 --> 00:02:02.791
<b>When we accept that happiness and joy are </b>
<b>not dependent on success or failure,</b>

20
00:02:02.791 --> 00:02:09.208
<b>we naturally begin to live a free and peaceful life.</b>

21
00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:16.041
<b>Consider the analogy of a gardener who </b>
<b>finds joy in the process of gardening itself.</b>

22
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:25.250
<b>He plants seeds, waters them, tends </b>
<b>to the garden, and nurtures the plants.</b>

23
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:29.583
<b>Naturally, some plants grow, some don't;</b>

24
00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:32.750
<b>some bloom, some don't.</b>

25
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.041
<b>But this does not affect the gardener's dedication.</b>

26
00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:42.958
<b>Whether a plant grows well or not,</b>

27
00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:48.458
<b>he continues his work without sorrow, </b>
<b>continuing to nurture.</b>

28
00:02:48.458 --> 00:02:53.083
<b>Because true joy lies in the process of action itself.</b>

29
00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:56.958
<b>Similarly, a human should not worry </b>
<b>about the outcome</b>

30
00:02:56.958 --> 00:03:00.541
<b>and perform their duties with </b>
<b>complete dedication,</b>

31
00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:03.208
<b>Lord Krishna emphasizes that one </b>
<b>should perform actions</b>

32
00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:07.416
<b>with the goals of self-satisfaction and </b>
<b>freedom.</b>

33
00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:14.541
<b>This is a state where you are not dependent </b>
<b>on any external causes for your happiness.</b>

34
00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:17.916
<b>You experience contentment within yourself.</b>

35
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:23.791
<b>When you are not subject to any external </b>
<b>circumstance, person, or result,</b>

36
00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:26.583
<b>that is true liberation, isn’t it?</b>

37
00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:32.875
<b>In such a state, no bonds constrain you. </b>
<b>To act without being bound –</b>

38
00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:35.958
<b>this is the essence of actionless action.</b>

39
00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:39.166
<b>This is why Sri Krishna says that such a person,</b>

40
00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:44.375
<b>while performing various actions, is actually </b>
<b>not performing any action at all.</b>

41
00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:47.833
<b>In practical terms, the core message is:</b>

42
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:50.833
<b>Find joy in your work</b>

43
00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:53.416
<b>Seek satisfaction in the process</b>

44
00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:56.125
<b>Make every effort with complete dedication</b>

45
00:03:56.125 --> 00:03:57.125
<b>And then</b>

46
00:03:57.125 --> 00:04:02.333
<b>completely renounce the desire</b>
<b>and anxiety about the results.</b>

47
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:09.416
<b>In this verse,</b>

48
00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:13.708
<b>I reveal a profound secret –</b>

49
00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:18.125
<b>the art of liberation from the bondage of action.</b>

50
00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:23.083
<b>This secret is hidden in three</b>
<b>fundamental principles:</b>

51
00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:26.500
<b>Perform your tasks without anxiety </b>
<b>about their outcomes.</b>

52
00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.708
<b>Discover contentment within yourself.</b>

53
00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:37.125
<b>Do not allow the joy of your life to be dependent </b>
<b>on external circumstances or influences.</b>

54
00:04:37.125 --> 00:04:41.583
<b>Let's understand this practically:</b>

55
00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:47.375
<b>If you find satisfaction in what you currently have,</b>

56
00:04:47.375 --> 00:04:48.333
<b>then</b>

57
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:53.541
<b>the desire for new fruits from new </b>
<b>actions will not torment you.</b>

58
00:04:53.541 --> 00:04:59.416
<b>Yes, I know, you might wonder,</b>

59
00:04:59.416 --> 00:05:03.500
<b>"Does this mean I should </b>
<b>stop striving for progress?"</b>

60
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.958
<b>Understand this clearly –</b>

61
00:05:05.958 --> 00:05:10.416
<b>it does not mean you should cease your efforts.</b>

62
00:05:10.416 --> 00:05:11.583
<b>Strive,</b>

63
00:05:11.583 --> 00:05:12.791
<b>absolutely strive,</b>

64
00:05:12.791 --> 00:05:18.041
<b>but do not bind your happiness </b>
<b>and sorrow to the results.</b>

65
00:05:18.041 --> 00:05:20.500
<b>Consider this example: </b>

66
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:28.041
<b>When you exercise, you experience an </b>
<b>energy in your body that feels good.</b>

67
00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:32.875
<b>At this moment, you are satisfied with </b>
<b>the action itself, with the process.</b>

68
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.583
<b>You perform this action daily,</b>

69
00:05:35.583 --> 00:05:36.458
<b>but</b>

70
00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:40.375
<b>you don't scrutinize yourself</b>
<b>in the mirror every day</b>

71
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:43.041
<b>to see how beautiful your body has become.</b>

72
00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:46.708
<b>When satisfaction comes from the action itself,</b>

73
00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:51.208
<b>you become free from outcomes.</b>

74
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:57.625
<b>To develop such thoughts, </b>
<b>practice gratitude daily.</b>

75
00:05:57.625 --> 00:05:59.875
<b>Instead of comparing yourself to others</b>

76
00:05:59.875 --> 00:06:03.291
<b>or complaining about what you lack,</b>

77
00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:10.333
<b>hold and express gratitude for what you have.</b>

78
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:12.416
<b>Imagine</b>

79
00:06:12.416 --> 00:06:15.333
<b>how beautiful this perspective is –</b>

80
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:18.500
<b>where you are grateful in every moment.</b>

81
00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.291
<b>Grateful for the food you've consumed today,</b>

82
00:06:22.291 --> 00:06:25.583
<b>for the family that stands by you,</b>

83
00:06:25.583 --> 00:06:28.666
<b>for the life you've been given,</b>

84
00:06:28.666 --> 00:06:29.416
<b>and</b>

85
00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:37.666
<b>for the education that helps you read </b>
<b>and understand this verse.</b>

86
00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:49.375
<b>The spiritual perspective teaches that desire</b>
<b>never brings contentment – gratitude does.</b>

87
00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.083
<b>Remain always grateful,</b>

88
00:06:51.083 --> 00:06:52.083
<b>and yes,</b>

89
00:06:52.083 --> 00:06:57.333
<b>find joy in the process of whatever </b>
<b>action you undertake –</b>

90
00:06:57.333 --> 00:07:04.625
<b>be it exercise, cooking, spending time </b>
<b>with loved ones,</b>

91
00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:06.333
<b>or anything else.</b>

92
00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:12.750
<b>Watch how anxiety diminishes and joy increases.</b>

93
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.833
<b>Contemplate this</b>

94
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:18.083
<b>and follow it.</b>

95
00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:24.791
<b>This verse</b>

96
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:27.333
<b>is about self-satisfaction</b>

97
00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:34.250
<b>and being self-reliant to experience joy in life.</b>

98
00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:39.375
<b>A significant part of family life is</b>

99
00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:44.333
<b>emotional interdependence on each other.</b>

100
00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:46.041
<b>However,</b>

101
00:07:46.041 --> 00:07:52.625
<b>when this dependency becomes excessive,</b>

102
00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:55.791
<b>it creates stress,</b>

103
00:07:55.791 --> 00:08:00.708
<b>making the relationship feel like a burden.</b>

104
00:08:00.708 --> 00:08:10.041
<b>If you truly love your family, </b>
<b>your children, your life partner –</b>

105
00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:12.500
<b>what would you want?</b>

106
00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:20.208
<b>Would you want them to always remain </b>
<b>dependent on others for their happiness?</b>

107
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:25.916
<b>Or would you want them to </b>
<b>remain happy and self-reliant?</b>

108
00:08:25.916 --> 00:08:28.916
<b>Understand this correctly.</b>

109
00:08:28.916 --> 00:08:30.875
<b>It never means that</b>

110
00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:38.791
<b>in a family one should not seek help during </b>
<b>difficult times or not support each other.</b>

111
00:08:38.791 --> 00:08:44.083
<b>Supporting each other in sorrow is </b>
<b>the foundation of family.</b>

112
00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:45.916
<b>But</b>

113
00:08:45.916 --> 00:08:49.375
<b>who can provide the best support </b>
<b>during difficult times?</b>

114
00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:51.166
<b>One who is self-reliant,</b>

115
00:08:51.166 --> 00:08:56.208
<b>not someone who is dependent </b>
<b>on others for their own happiness.</b>

116
00:08:56.208 --> 00:09:01.916
<b>Just as only a strong person</b>
<b>can help lift heavy luggage,</b>

117
00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:03.416
<b>not a weak one,</b>

118
00:09:03.416 --> 00:09:04.625
<b>similarly,</b>

119
00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:12.416
<b>only those who are self-sufficient can provide </b>
<b>better support during challenging times.</b>

120
00:09:12.416 --> 00:09:16.125
<b>Being emotionally strong</b>

121
00:09:16.125 --> 00:09:17.875
<b>is not selfishness.</b>

122
00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:24.666
<b>Only those who are emotionally </b>
<b>stable can help others.</b>

123
00:09:24.666 --> 00:09:25.708
<b>Now</b>

124
00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:29.416
<b>imagine a beautiful family</b>

125
00:09:29.416 --> 00:09:33.541
<b>where everyone loves each other deeply,</b>

126
00:09:33.541 --> 00:09:38.833
<b>and everyone strives to be emotionally strong</b>

127
00:09:38.833 --> 00:09:44.250
<b>so that they can support others </b>
<b>during challenging moments.</b>

128
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.875
<b>Isn't this also a form of service?</b>

129
00:09:47.875 --> 00:09:49.083
<b>Therefore,</b>

130
00:09:49.083 --> 00:09:52.250
<b>always try to remain happy.</b>

131
00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:58.000
<b>Simultaneously, inspire others to live such a life.</b>

132
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.375
<b>There are many ways to do this:</b>

133
00:09:59.375 --> 00:10:03.291
<b>just like finding joy in positive interests,</b>

134
00:10:03.291 --> 00:10:04.625
<b>exercising –</b>

135
00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:06.000
<b>remember,</b>

136
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.416
<b>a healthy body houses a healthy mind.</b>

137
00:10:10.416 --> 00:10:11.833
<b>Also,</b>

138
00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:18.625
<b>the paths of spirituality, meditation, </b>
<b>and self-reflection are also open to you.</b>

139
00:10:18.625 --> 00:10:20.375
<b>Many paths exist –</b>

140
00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:26.375
<b>walk them yourself and inspire </b>
<b>others to walk them too.</b>

141
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.375
<b>Finding satisfaction in one's work</b>

142
00:10:34.375 --> 00:10:41.916
<b>without depending on any </b>
<b>external object, person, or circumstance –</b>

143
00:10:41.916 --> 00:10:45.625
<b>this is what this verse speaks about.</b>

144
00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:49.708
<b>This is emotional freedom.</b>

145
00:10:49.708 --> 00:10:52.291
<b>In a workplace, this means</b>

146
00:10:52.291 --> 00:10:54.666
<b>engaging in your work with dedication,</b>

147
00:10:54.666 --> 00:10:58.458
<b>finding inspiration and satisfaction</b>
<b>in the work itself,</b>

148
00:10:58.458 --> 00:11:00.125
<b>without thinking about</b>

149
00:11:00.125 --> 00:11:07.875
<b>what reward you'll receive or whether </b>
<b>you'll be praised or not.</b>

150
00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:16.500
<b>When you complete an important </b>
<b>project or a challenging task, you feel pride.</b>

151
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:23.625
<b>And the root source of this pride is </b>
<b>the satisfaction of doing the work well.</b>

152
00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:25.166
<b>Consider:</b>

153
00:11:25.166 --> 00:11:31.875
<b>If you contribute nothing but </b>
<b>mistakenly receive praise,</b>

154
00:11:31.875 --> 00:11:35.500
<b>you'll feel incomplete, wouldn’t you?</b>

155
00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.541
<b>Conversely,</b>

156
00:11:36.541 --> 00:11:40.166
<b>if you work hard and succeed,</b>

157
00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:44.916
<b>whether you receive recognition or not,</b>

158
00:11:44.916 --> 00:11:48.666
<b>your self-satisfaction remains.</b>

159
00:11:48.666 --> 00:11:50.625
<b>Because you know</b>

160
00:11:50.625 --> 00:11:54.458
<b>you performed the task with full commitment.</b>

161
00:11:54.458 --> 00:11:58.416
<b>Dedication in work is a kind of freedom</b>

162
00:11:58.416 --> 00:12:02.208
<b>that liberates you from disappointment.</b>

163
00:12:02.208 --> 00:12:03.458
<b>in such a case, </b>

164
00:12:03.458 --> 00:12:10.666
<b>your happiness is not dependent on others, </b>
<b>nor on their appreciation.</b>

165
00:12:10.666 --> 00:12:16.458
<b>You experience joy in the process of work itself.</b>

166
00:12:16.458 --> 00:12:21.916
<b>Therefore, let go of anxiety about results </b>
<b>and enjoy the process.</b>

167
00:12:21.916 --> 00:12:26.500
<b>Take pride in the fact that you did the work well,</b>

168
00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.750
<b>learned something new,</b>

169
00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:33.208
<b>and perhaps helped someone </b>
<b>else through your work.</b>

170
00:12:33.208 --> 00:12:37.708
<b>This is the path of true contentment.</b>

